            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0714" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.857/58: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-27T20:00:00-05:00">February 27,
                            1940—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Department’s 39, February 26, 6 p.m. In order to expedite this matter, the
                    Department suggests that the Brazilian Government circulate the text of the
                    protest on the <hi rendition="#italic">Wakama</hi> incident drafted by that
                    Government to the other American Republics for their approval. Please inform
                    Aranha that the Department will be pleased to assist in this matter,
                    particularly in the case of countries where Brazil has no diplomatic
                    representation. In view of the time which has elapsed since this incident, it is
                    felt that the matter should be handled by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
